      "writtenOn": "2020-02-13T15:50:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This entire section is a change-detector test.\n\n• It requires that there is an executor, that all processing must be sent to it, that none of the enqueued runnables should enqueue another (otherwise the latch exits before the queue is indeed finished processing). None of this is part of the contract of the class, and indeed can be changed easily without violating said contract, but that will require deep changes to the test.\n• It tests that private members are reset. This is none of the business of anyone outside of the runner, not even this test. In fact, before the previous patchset, as you noticed the legacy test runner did NOT reset these, and it was working well enough.\n\nI think this entire section should be removed. Instead test a visible side effect : that the network agent has disconnected, and/or that the interface has been downed or something like that. It is more useful, more effective, costs less maintenance and lets you remove the uncomfortable exposure of these private members.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1057,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1068,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "e9b779f16f39aa5995934e48750a8fa4974b6137",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
